8fS8fAltaUOavyrlgBo6zPLw85NbANYSktiRRuOOrejKiQSgAmcqtBdrnu8V_h2hhFVw7N5FVhYxYg-05I6Nx7czS7nmbiIEQohN3Gbkx9XaZEpopifcIeaTDijKcB3rolihk635_WniYeCXpNDSbajE8kYtiIYa7qWtUbjyxoaXj7BsagnRNlaYxXun0_73MC5xEvfcuRbrWFKxsCdaBzo94X1ZheE0Tpjc7SungAZO402_aLrrE11M6GADRsvGTCwPkWHHOSI4IdrW87MWoxEZGFexgsJ38tcxIIDVcQCzdBo0LnzfZp_4v0HqRNyRLllPYX2E2lmYRehl8VZ-YwpZ7ZyTZii7LxE3wznAhPmUbn_SCw2Bg6FyAA8JEKcUkqNeTpcFg39toqzdkiZR8JeaGXzUTIFgBkN7t9euieISjHE1k8yB28k6GSUoE9zL7Q4PoQ6Rw04-WCmo6wynSq9uK7LSet6-5hmAjy3YfV0NIuhjH6G8GX_Nm4L8abuL9Rr4y9PSZjynM0OnXP"},{"type":"message","id":"msg_0c3f58f1d426e40d016adf58f9c5508191b844add2c776ea5a","role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’ve read the complete supplied proof, including the zero-dimensional ambient case. I’m organizing it into explicit units for the Hausdorff-measure conventions, finite-dimensional bound, product-cover upper bound, slicing estimate, and two lower-bound cases. I’ve also checked the pinned library statements for the main Hausdorff-dimension, integration, and interval-length tools; their applications still need to be justified in the artifact.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0c3f58f1d426e40d016adf58fd05f88191850c488a339765ea","call_id":"call_cc20b798711647d2abe4654be7c347de","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"spec\":{\"format_version\":2,\"case_id\":\"geometry-product-dimension\",\"full_target\":\"Let n≥0 be an integer and let E⊆ℝ^n be nonempty and compact. Put I=[0,1] and identify ℝ^n×ℝ with ℝ^{n+1}, using the Euclidean metric. Prove dim_H(E×[0,1])=dim_H(E)+1, including n=0. Hausdorff measure is the unnormalized countable-diameter-cover measure specified below and dim_H(∅)=0.\",\"conclusion\":\"hdim(F)=hdim(E)+1.\",\"parameters\":[{\"symbol\":\"n\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"E\",\"type\":\"subset of Euclidean ℝ^n\"}],\"hypotheses\":[{\"id\":\"H001\",\"statement\":\"E is nonempty.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:16-23; the disclosed approved nonemptiness assumption.\"},{\"id\":\"H002\",\"statement\":\"E is compact.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:21-23; original compactness assumption.\"}],\"definitions\":[{\"id\":\"D001\",\"symbol\":\"I\",\"type\":\"subset of ℝ\",\"definition\":\"I=[0,1]={t∈ℝ:0≤t≤1}.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"id\":\"D002\",\"symbol\":\"F\",\"type\":\"subset of Euclidean ℝ^{n+1}, identified with ℝ^n×ℝ\",\"definition\":\"F=E×I. Under the coordinate identification (x,t)↔(x_1,…,x_n,t), the distance between (x,t) and (y,u) is sqrt(‖x-y‖₂²+|t-u|²). For n=0, ℝ^0 consists of its unique empty coordinate vector.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D001\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"point of ℝ^n\"},{\"symbol\":\"y\",\"type\":\"point of ℝ^n\"},{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"u\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"E\",\"I\",\"x\",\"y\",\"t\",\"u\"]},{\"id\":\"D003\",\"symbol\":\"Hscale\",\"type\":\"operator on a metric space X, a positive real s, a positive real δ and a subset A⊆X, valued in [0,∞]\",\"definition\":\"For a metric space X, s>0, δ>0 and A⊆X, Hscale(s,δ,A)=inf{Σ_{i≥0}(diam U_i)^s : A⊆⋃_{i≥0}U_i and diam U_i≤δ for every i}. Covers are countable (finite covers are padded by empty sets). The diameter is the supremum of pairwise distances, with diameter of the empty set zero and unbounded diameter +∞; an empty member contributes zero. Sums, infima and suprema are in [0,∞], with inf ∅=∞. Covers are not required to be measurable.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"},{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of X\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"A\",\"U\"]},{\"id\":\"D004\",\"symbol\":\"Hmeasure\",\"type\":\"operator on positive real exponents and subsets of metric spaces, valued in [0,∞]\",\"definition\":\"For s>0 and a subset A of a metric space X, Hmeasure(s,A)=sup_{δ>0}Hscale(s,δ,A). This is precisely the unnormalized Hausdorff measure convention in problem.md:34-42.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D003\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"s\",\"A\",\"Hscale\"]},{\"id\":\"D008\",\"symbol\":\"Hnative\",\"type\":\"operator on a real exponent a and a subset A of an extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, valued in [0,∞]\",\"definition\":\"Hnative(a,A) denotes the native value (MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure a)(A) on X. Its full covering formula is sup_{r∈(0,∞]} inf_{T:ℕ→Set X, A⊆⋃_i T_i, ∀i ediam(T_i)≤r} Σ_i w_a(T_i), where w_a(T)=0 for T empty and w_a(T)=(ediam T)^a otherwise; all diameters and operations here are extended nonnegative real operations, including extended real powers. Thus empty sets are zero even at exponent zero. The native definition is the Borel measure Measure.mkMetric(r↦r^a); M001 verifies the displayed covering formula. For ordinary metric spaces ediam is the extended-valued supremum of ordinary distances.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"extended metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"a\",\"A\"]},{\"id\":\"D005\",\"symbol\":\"hdim\",\"type\":\"operator on subsets of metric spaces, valued in [0,∞]\",\"definition\":\"For A⊆X, hdim(A)=sup{a∈[0,∞):Hnative(a,A)=∞}, with the empty supremum equal to zero and real exponents embedded into [0,∞]. This is the native dimH definition (the exponent is represented by a nonnegative real). It is the usual Hausdorff dimension; in particular the definition assigns zero to the empty set.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D008\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"Hnative\"]},{\"id\":\"D006\",\"symbol\":\"D\",\"type\":\"extended nonnegative real number\",\"definition\":\"D=hdim(E). Once finiteness is proved, real arithmetic with D means its unique finite real representative; no finiteness is assumed by this definition.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D005\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"hdim\"]}],\"logic\":{\"classical\":true,\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"case_elimination\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\"]},\"pins\":{},\"inputs\":[]},\"graph\":{\"format_version\":2,\"case_id\":\"geometry-product-dimension\",\"spec_sha256\":\"controller-bound\",\"propositions\":[{\"id\":\"H001\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\"]},{\"id\":\"H002\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\"]},{\"id\":\"M001\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every extended metric space X with a measurable space structure equal to its Borel structure, every real a and every A⊆X, Hnative(a,A)=sup_{r∈[0,∞], r>0} inf_{T:ℕ→Set X, A⊆⋃_i T_i, ∀i ediam(T_i)≤r} Σ_i sup_{h:T_i.Nonempty}(ediam(T_i))^a. The inner supremum is zero for an empty T_i and is the indicated power otherwise.\",\"definitions\":[\"D008\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"extended metric space with a Borel measurable structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"a\",\"A\",\"Hnative\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure_apply\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is an extended metric space.\",\"X has a measurable space structure and this structure is its Borel structure.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M002\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, A⊆X and nonnegative real a, if a<hdim(A), then Hnative(a,A)=∞.\",\"definitions\":[\"D005\",\"D008\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"extended metric space with a Borel measurable structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"},{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"nonnegative real\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"a\",\"hdim\",\"Hnative\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is an extended metric space.\",\"X has a measurable space structure equal to its Borel structure.\",\"a is a nonnegative real and a<hdim(A).\"]}},{\"id\":\"M003\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, A⊆X and nonnegative real a, if hdim(A)<a, then Hnative(a,A)=0.\",\"definitions\":[\"D005\",\"D008\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"extended metric space with a Borel measurable structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"},{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"nonnegative real\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"a\",\"hdim\",\"Hnative\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"hausdorffMeasure_of_dimH_lt\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is an extended metric space.\",\"X has a measurable space structure equal to its Borel structure.\",\"a is a nonnegative real and hdim(A)<a.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M004\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, A⊆X and nonnegative real a, if Hnative(a,A)≠∞, then hdim(A)≤a.\",\"definitions\":[\"D005\",\"D008\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"extended metric space with a Borel measurable structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"},{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"nonnegative real\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"a\",\"hdim\",\"Hnative\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"dimH_le_of_hausdorffMeasure_ne_top\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is an extended metric space.\",\"X has a measurable space structure equal to its Borel structure.\",\"a is a nonnegative real and Hnative(a,A)≠∞.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M005\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"Let α be a measurable space, μ a measure on α, β a countable type and f:β→α→[0,∞]. If every f_i is μ-almost-everywhere measurable, then ∫⁻_α Σ_{i:β} f_i(a) dμ(a)=Σ_{i:β} ∫⁻_α f_i(a) dμ(a).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"α\",\"type\":\"measurable space\"},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"measure on α\"},{\"symbol\":\"β\",\"type\":\"countable type\"},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"β→α→[0,∞]\"}],\"objects\":[\"α\",\"μ\",\"β\",\"f\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\",\"hypotheses\":[\"α has a measurable space structure and μ is a measure on it.\",\"β is countable.\",\"For every i∈β, f_i is μ-almost-everywhere measurable.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M006\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any type α, index type ι, a type G of set functions on α equipped with a FunLike structure into [0,∞] and an OuterMeasureClass structure, any μ∈G, and any family T:ι→Set α, if ι is countable then μ(⋃_{i:ι}T_i)≤Σ_{i:ι}μ(T_i).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"α\",\"type\":\"type\"},{\"symbol\":\"ι\",\"type\":\"countable type\"},{\"symbol\":\"G\",\"type\":\"type with FunLike G (Set α) [0,∞] and OuterMeasureClass G α\"},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"element of G\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"ι→Set α\"}],\"objects\":[\"α\",\"ι\",\"G\",\"μ\",\"T\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"MeasureTheory.measure_iUnion_le\",\"hypotheses\":[\"G has the stated FunLike and OuterMeasureClass structures, and μ is an element of G.\",\"ι is countable.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M007\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any real endpoints a,b, Lebesgue measure of the closed interval [a,b] is ENNReal.ofReal(b-a), namely max(b-a,0) embedded in [0,∞].\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Real.volume_Icc\",\"hypotheses\":[]}},{\"id\":\"M008\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For any real endpoints a,b, Lebesgue measure of the open interval (a,b) is ENNReal.ofReal(b-a), namely max(b-a,0) embedded in [0,∞].\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"real number\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Real.volume_Ioo\",\"hypotheses\":[]}},{\"id\":\"N001\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"For every metric space X, every A⊆X and every real s>0, Hmeasure(s,A)=Hnative(s,A). Moreover Hmeasure(s,A)=0 if hdim(A)<s; Hmeasure(s,A)=∞ if s<hdim(A); Hmeasure(s,A)=0 implies hdim(A)≤s; and Hmeasure(s,A)=∞ implies s≤hdim(A).\",\"definitions\":[\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D008\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"metric space\"},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"s\",\"Hmeasure\",\"Hnative\",\"hdim\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:34-47; explicit normalization and critical-exponent bridge.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"E is bounded. For every δ>0 and every s>0, E has a finite cover by sets of diameter at most δ and finite s-cost, so Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞. Also 0≤D≤n, in particular hdim(E)=D is finite and can be identified with a real number. If n=0, then E=ℝ^0 is the singleton and D=0.\",\"definitions\":[\"D003\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"}],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"δ\",\"s\",\"D\",\"Hscale\",\"hdim\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:49-57 and 130-131.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"hdim(F)≤D+1.\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"F\",\"D\",\"hdim\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:59-92, with positive-diameter cover preparation retained.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"For every real s>0 and every real δ>0, Hscale(s,δ,E)≤Hscale(s+1,δ,F).\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D003\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real\"}],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"δ\",\"E\",\"F\",\"Hscale\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:98-147; the complete slicing estimate.\"},{\"id\":\"N005\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"If D>0, then hdim(F)≥D+1.\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"F\",\"hdim\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:94-149.\"},{\"id\":\"N006\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"If D=0, then hdim(F)≥1=D+1, including n=0.\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"F\",\"n\",\"hdim\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:151-165; interval dimension and isometric embedded copy.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"kind\":\"target\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D005\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"F\",\"E\",\"hdim\"]}],\"inferences\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"inputs\":[\"M001\",\"M002\",\"M003\",\"M004\"],\"output\":\"N001\",\"definitions\":[\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D008\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"metric space\",\"scope\":\"R001/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary metric space X, equipped for source applications with its Borel σ algebra.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"subset of X\",\"scope\":\"R001/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary subset A of X.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"X\"]},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R001/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix s>0 for the universally quantified assertion.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Fix a metric space X, a subset A⊆X and s>0. Regard its metric as an extended metric and give X its Borel measurable structure. M001 gives the native covering formula. At every finite positive scale its inner infimum is exactly Hscale(s,δ,A): extended diameter agrees with ordinary diameter on bounded sets, nonempty-member costs agree, and both conventions make empty members zero. Infinite-diameter sets cannot occur at a finite scale. The extra scale r=∞ in M001 contributes no more than any finite-scale infimum because its cover class is larger. Thus its inclusion does not change the supremum over finite positive scales. Hence Hnative(s,A)=Hmeasure(s,A).\",\"uses\":[\"M001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"s\",\"Hnative\",\"Hmeasure\",\"Hscale\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"For the arbitrary X,A and s>0, Hnative(s,A)=Hmeasure(s,A).\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"s\",\"Hnative\",\"Hmeasure\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Using F001, apply M002 in the case s<hdim(A) to obtain Hmeasure(s,A)=∞. Apply M003 in the case hdim(A)<s to obtain Hmeasure(s,A)=0. If Hmeasure(s,A)=0, F001 makes Hnative(s,A)=0≠∞, so M004 gives hdim(A)≤s. If Hmeasure(s,A)=∞, then F001 and the supremum definition of hdim show s≤hdim(A), since s is one of its nonnegative exponents with infinite native measure. Each implication is conditional only on its displayed antecedent and is closed here; X,A,s were arbitrary. This proves every clause of N001.\",\"uses\":[\"M002\",\"M003\",\"M004\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"A\",\"s\",\"Hnative\",\"Hmeasure\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\",\"L4\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\",\"L2\",\"L3\",\"L4\"]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"Use the current metric space X as an extended metric space, a=s and the current subset A.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"The metric of X gives its extended metric by embedding each distance into [0,∞].\",\"Equip X with exactly its Borel σ algebra, so both measurable-space and BorelSpace premises hold.\"]},{\"input\":\"M002\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"Use X,A as in S001 and the nonnegative real exponent a=s.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"X has the extended metric fixed in S001.\",\"The measurable structure was chosen to be the Borel structure in S001.\",\"s>0 was fixed in S001, so it is a nonnegative real; the local antecedent of this implication is s<hdim(A).\"]},{\"input\":\"M003\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"Use X,A as in S001 and a=s.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"X has the extended metric fixed in S001.\",\"X has its Borel measurable structure by S001.\",\"s>0 makes s nonnegative; this implication has antecedent hdim(A)<s.\"]},{\"input\":\"M004\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"Use X,A as in S001 and a=s in the implication whose antecedent is Hmeasure(s,A)=0.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"X has the extended metric fixed in S001.\",\"X has its Borel measurable structure by S001.\",\"s>0 makes s nonnegative, and F001 changes the local zero-measure antecedent into Hnative(s,A)=0, which is not ∞.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"N001\"],\"output\":\"N002\",\"definitions\":[\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"case_elimination\",\"forall_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"B\",\"type\":\"positive real number\",\"scope\":\"R002/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Let B≥1 be a bound for the norms of E obtained in S001 from a finite subcover of the integer-radius balls.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H002\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"By H002 and the finite-open-subcover definition of compactness, the increasing open balls about 0 of positive integer radii have a finite subcover of E. These balls cover Euclidean space because every point has finite norm. The maximum of their radii, enlarged to at least 1, is a finite number B with ‖x‖₂≤B for all x∈E. This proves boundedness. Also, for any δ>0, the open balls of radius δ/2 about points of E form an open cover; compactness supplies a finite subcover. Each ball has diameter at most δ by the triangle inequality and hence finite s-cost for every s>0. A finite sum of these costs is finite, so the defining infimum gives Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞.\",\"uses\":[\"H002\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"B\",\"Hscale\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"‖x‖₂≤B for all x∈E, and for all δ>0 and s>0 one has Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"point of E\"},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"positive real\"}],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"B\",\"Hscale\",\"x\",\"δ\",\"s\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Always D≥0 by its extended-nonnegative-real definition. If n>0, E lies in the box [-B,B]^n by F001. For each 0<h≤1, use the ordinary grid of mesh h and retain cubes intersecting this box. There are at most (2B/h+3)^n≤(2B+3)^n h^{-n} such cubes, each of side h and Euclidean diameter at most √n h (sum the n coordinate squared differences). Writing C=(2B+3)^n, for every real exponent a>n their total a-cost is at most C n^{a/2}h^{a-n}→0 as h↓0. At any fixed target scale, all sufficiently small h are admissible and these costs tend to zero; thus Hscale(a,δ,E)=0 for every δ>0 and Hmeasure(a,E)=0. N001 gives D≤a for every a>n, hence D≤n. If n=0, H001 makes E the whole singleton ℝ^0. Its singleton cover has zero s-cost for every s>0 at every positive scale. N001 gives D≤s for all s>0, hence D=0. This proves the claimed bound and the exceptional-case identification; since n is finite, D is finite. Together with S001 this proves N002.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"B\",\"D\",\"hdim\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"]}],\"applications\":[]},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"inputs\":[\"N001\",\"N002\"],\"output\":\"N003\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"case_elimination\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"q\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"In the branch n≥1, fix an arbitrary real q>D.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N002\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\"]},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary target scale δ>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary ε>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"positive real number\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define r=min(1,δ/√2)>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"δ\"]},{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"countable family of nonempty subsets of ℝ^n\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose a cover U of E with positive diameters at most r and total q-cost less than ε, whose existence is F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\",\"r\",\"q\",\"ε\"]},{\"symbol\":\"r_i\",\"type\":\"family of positive real numbers indexed by the countable index set of U\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For each cover index i, define r_i=diam U_i.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"U\"]},{\"symbol\":\"N_i\",\"type\":\"family of positive integers indexed by the index set of U\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define N_i=ceil(1/r_i).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"r_i\"]},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"countable family of subsets of ℝ^{n+1} indexed by pairs (i,j), 1≤j≤N_i\",\"scope\":\"R003/positive-ambient-case\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define T_{i,j}=U_i×[(j-1)/N_i,j/N_i].\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"N_i\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"First suppose n=0. N002 gives E=ℝ^0 and D=0. With the Euclidean metric in D002, F is isometric to I. For each positive integer N, divide I into N closed pieces of length 1/N and use their copies in F. For any a>1, their total a-cost is N(1/N)^a=N^{1-a}→0 as N→∞, while their diameters tend to zero. Thus at each target scale Hscale(a,δ,F)=0 and Hmeasure(a,F)=0. N001 gives hdim(F)≤a for all a>1, so hdim(F)≤1=D+1. This closes the n=0 branch.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"E\",\"D\",\"F\",\"I\",\"hdim\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[\"L1\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Now suppose n≥1. N002 permits regarding D as a finite real number. Fix q>D, a target scale δ>0 and ε>0, and set r=min(1,δ/√2). Since D≥0, q>0. N001 gives Hmeasure(q,E)=0, hence Hscale(q,r,E)=0. The definition of infimum supplies a countable r-cover of cost less than ε/2. Delete empty members. Every remaining diameter-zero member is a singleton. Replace its member with original index i≥0 by a ball centered at that singleton, of positive diameter at most r and q-cost less than ε2^{-i-2}. Such a ball exists in ℝ^n for n≥1: take a sufficiently small positive radius, using (2a)^q→0 as a↓0. The sum of all added costs is at most Σ_{i≥0}ε2^{-i-2}=ε/2, and in fact the resulting total cost is less than ε. Keep the positive-diameter original members. This proves the existence of a countable cover of E with every member nonempty, 0<diam U_i≤r and Σ_i(diam U_i)^q<ε.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"E\",\"D\",\"q\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"r\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There exists a countable cover U of E by nonempty sets with 0<diam U_i≤r and Σ_i(diam U_i)^q<ε.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"countable family of subsets of ℝ^n\"}],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"E\",\"n\",\"q\",\"r\",\"ε\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L2\",\"L3\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Choose U by F001, and put r_i=diam U_i and N_i=ceil(1/r_i). Partition I into the N_i closed intervals [(j-1)/N_i,j/N_i], 1≤j≤N_i. They have length 1/N_i≤r_i. As 0<r_i≤r≤1, one has N_i≤1/r_i+1≤2/r_i. The sets T_{i,j}=U_i×[(j-1)/N_i,j/N_i] form a countable cover of F. The Euclidean product distance gives diam T_{i,j}≤√2 r_i≤δ. Their total (q+1)-cost is bounded by Σ_i N_i(√2 r_i)^{q+1}≤2(√2)^{q+1}Σ_i r_i^q<2(√2)^{q+1}ε. Consequently Hscale(q+1,δ,F)≤2(√2)^{q+1}ε.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"U\",\"r_i\",\"N_i\",\"T\",\"I\",\"F\",\"r\",\"δ\",\"q\",\"ε\",\"Hscale\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"Hscale(q+1,δ,F)≤2(√2)^{q+1}ε.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"Hscale\",\"q\",\"δ\",\"F\",\"ε\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L2\",\"L3\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"The bound F002 holds for every ε>0, at the arbitrary positive scale δ and arbitrary q>D. Taking ε↓0 gives Hscale(q+1,δ,F)=0. Taking the supremum over all δ>0 gives Hmeasure(q+1,F)=0, and N001 yields hdim(F)≤q+1 for every q>D. Since D is finite by N002, letting q↓D gives hdim(F)≤D+1 (equivalently, any larger number would admit an intermediate q+1 contradicting these bounds). Close the restrictions q>D, δ>0, ε>0 and the n≥1 case. Together with S001 this is N003.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"q\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"r\",\"U\",\"r_i\",\"N_i\",\"T\",\"D\",\"F\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L3\",\"L2\"]}],\"applications\":[]},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"inputs\":[\"N002\",\"M005\",\"M007\",\"M008\"],\"output\":\"N004\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix s>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix δ>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix ε>0, to be sent to zero.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"extended nonnegative real number\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define c=Hscale(s,δ,E).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"Hscale\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"E\"]},{\"symbol\":\"V\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of ℝ^{n+1}\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Take any countable δ-cover V of F, allowing empty padding members.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"δ\",\"F\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ρ\",\"type\":\"sequence of finite nonnegative real numbers\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define ρ_i=diam V_i; since V is a δ-cover, 0≤ρ_i≤δ.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"δ\"]},{\"symbol\":\"A_i\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of ℝ^n\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define A_i as the projection of V_i onto ℝ^n.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"B_i\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define B_i as the last-coordinate projection of V_i.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\"]},{\"symbol\":\"η\",\"type\":\"sequence of positive real numbers\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"ε\",\"ρ\",\"s\"]},{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"sequence of open subsets of ℝ, each empty or a bounded open interval\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"If V_i is nonempty, set J_i=(inf B_i-η_i/2,sup B_i+η_i/2); otherwise set J_i=∅.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"B_i\",\"η\"]},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"ℕ→ℝ→[0,∞]\",\"scope\":\"R004/arbitrary-cover\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define f_i(t)=ρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t), with the nonnegative real coefficient embedded in [0,∞].\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"ρ\",\"s\",\"J\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Fix s>0, δ>0 and ε>0. Define c=Hscale(s,δ,E). N002 gives a finite δ-cover of E with finite s-cost, so c<∞. Thus c can be integrated as a finite nonnegative constant.\",\"uses\":[\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"c\",\"E\",\"Hscale\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"c=Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"Hscale\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"E\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Take any countable δ-cover V of F and write ρ_i=diam V_i, A_i=π_{ℝ^n}(V_i), B_i=π_ℝ(V_i). Coordinate projections decrease distances by the Euclidean distance formula; therefore diam A_i≤ρ_i and diam B_i≤ρ_i≤δ. Set η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s)>0. For every nonempty V_i its projection B_i is nonempty and bounded: distances between all its points are at most δ, so its infimum and supremum are finite. Their difference is at most ρ_i. Define J_i=(inf B_i-η_i/2,sup B_i+η_i/2), which contains B_i and has length at most ρ_i+η_i. For empty V_i set J_i=∅; such members have ρ_i^s=0 and are harmless. This is the same as discarding empty members while retaining the original indices. Thus every J_i is open and B_i⊆J_i. Neither V_i nor its projections need be measurable.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"F\",\"δ\",\"ρ\",\"A_i\",\"B_i\",\"η\",\"ε\",\"s\",\"J\",\"n\",\"c\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"For every i, diam A_i≤ρ_i≤δ, B_i⊆J_i, and J_i is either empty or an open interval of length at most ρ_i+η_i; η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s)>0.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"A_i\",\"B_i\",\"J\",\"ρ\",\"δ\",\"η\",\"ε\",\"s\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"For any t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E: for any x∈E some V_i contains (x,t), and then x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i. By F002 this is a δ-cover, whose s-cost is at most Σ_iρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Hence c≤Σ_iρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t) for every t∈I. Define f_i(t)=ρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Every f_i is nonnegative and Borel measurable because J_i is open and its coefficient is a fixed finite nonnegative real. In particular it is almost-everywhere measurable for Lebesgue measure restricted to I.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"E\",\"I\",\"F\",\"V\",\"A_i\",\"B_i\",\"J\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"f\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"For every t∈I, c≤Σ_i f_i(t), where f_i(t)=ρ_i^s1_{J_i}(t); each f_i is Borel measurable and hence Lebesgue-almost-everywhere measurable for the restricted measure on I.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"real number in I\"}],\"objects\":[\"t\",\"I\",\"c\",\"f\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"J\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"Integrate F003 against Lebesgue measure restricted to I. Its total mass is one by M007 with endpoints 0,1. Monotonicity of the nonnegative integral, the integral of a constant, and M005 applied to the nonnegative measurable series yield c≤Σ_i∫_I f_i(t)dt=Σ_iρ_i^s|J_i∩I|. Here the integral of a constant times a measurable indicator is that constant times its set's measure, directly the simple-function integral formula. By M008 and monotonicity of measure, |J_i∩I|≤|J_i|≤ρ_i+η_i (the empty case is zero). Consequently c≤Σ_iρ_i^s|J_i∩I|≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+Σ_iη_iρ_i^s≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε, because η_iρ_i^s=ε2^{-i-1}ρ_i^s/(1+ρ_i^s)≤ε2^{-i-1} and Σ_{i≥0}2^{-i-1}=1. All series are nonnegative; their order comparisons and splitting are valid also when a sum is infinite.\",\"uses\":[\"M005\",\"M007\",\"M008\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"I\",\"f\",\"J\",\"ρ\",\"η\",\"s\",\"ε\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε for the arbitrary δ-cover V and arbitrary ε>0.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"ε\",\"V\",\"δ\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"If Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}=∞, the desired bound c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1} is immediate. If the sum is finite, F004 for all ε>0 gives that bound by letting ε↓0. Since V was any δ-cover of F, taking the infimum of its (s+1)-costs gives Hscale(s,δ,E)=c≤Hscale(s+1,δ,F). The construction of J depended on ε, but c and this cover's cost did not, so the limit is legitimate. Discharge the arbitrary-cover restrictions and s>0,δ>0,ε>0 restrictions and universally quantify s,δ. This proves N004.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"ρ\",\"s\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"c\",\"E\",\"F\",\"J\",\"Hscale\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L2\",\"L1\"]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M005\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"Set α=ℝ with its Borel/Lebesgue measurable structure, μ=Lebesgue measure restricted to I, β=ℕ and use f_i from S003.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Lebesgue measure restricted to the Borel set I is a measure on this measurable space.\",\"The series index is ℕ, a countable type.\",\"F003 proves Borel measurability of every f_i, hence almost-everywhere measurability for μ.\"]},{\"input\":\"M007\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"Set a=0 and b=1; the interval [a,b] is I.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]},{\"input\":\"M008\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"For each nonempty V_i set a=inf B_i-η_i/2 and b=sup B_i+η_i/2, so (a,b)=J_i; empty members contribute zero separately.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]}]},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"inputs\":[\"N001\",\"N002\",\"N004\"],\"output\":\"N005\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R005/positive-D\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Under D>0 fix an arbitrary real s with 0<s<D.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N002\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Suppose D>0 and fix 0<s<D. By N001, Hmeasure(s,E)=∞. Thus Hscale(s,δ,E) is arbitrarily large as δ↓0: it increases when the allowed scale decreases, since the class of covers becomes smaller, and its supremum over positive scales is infinite. For every δ>0, N004 gives Hscale(s,δ,E)≤Hscale(s+1,δ,F). Therefore the supremum over scales on the right is infinite, so Hmeasure(s+1,F)=∞. N001 then gives hdim(F)≥s+1.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"N004\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"s\",\"E\",\"F\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"For every 0<s<D, hdim(F)≥s+1.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"real number\"}],\"objects\":[\"s\",\"D\",\"F\",\"hdim\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[\"L2\"]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"N002 makes D finite. Under D>0, the positive exponents s<D approach D from below. F001 therefore yields hdim(F)≥D+1 by order completeness; explicitly any number less than D+1 is less than s+1 for some 0<s<D. Close the assumption D>0 to obtain N005.\",\"uses\":[\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"s\",\"F\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]}],\"applications\":[]},{\"id\":\"R006\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"N001\",\"N002\",\"M006\",\"M007\",\"M008\"],\"output\":\"N006\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R006/interval-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"For the interval-cover assertion fix any δ>0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"real number\",\"scope\":\"R006/interval-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix any ε>0 for enlargement of an arbitrary interval cover.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[]},{\"symbol\":\"W\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R006/interval-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Take any countable δ-cover W of I, with empty padding allowed.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"δ\",\"I\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ρ\",\"type\":\"sequence of finite nonnegative real numbers\",\"scope\":\"R006/interval-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define ρ_i=diam W_i.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\"]},{\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"sequence of open subsets of ℝ\",\"scope\":\"R006/interval-cover\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"For nonempty W_i let J_i=(inf W_i-ε2^{-i-2},sup W_i+ε2^{-i-2}); for empty W_i set J_i=∅.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"ε\"]},{\"symbol\":\"x_0\",\"type\":\"point of ℝ^n belonging to E\",\"scope\":\"R006/zero-D\",\"start\":\"S004\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose x_0∈E by H001 in the branch D=0.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"E\",\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"φ\",\"type\":\"map from I to F\",\"scope\":\"R006/zero-D\",\"start\":\"S004\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define φ(t)=(x_0,t) for t∈I.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"F\",\"x_0\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"First establish the dimension of I. For every positive integer N its subdivision into N equal closed intervals is a cover with diameters 1/N. For every a>1, its total a-cost is N^{1-a}→0 as N→∞. These covers have mesh tending to zero, so Hmeasure(a,I)=0. By N001, hdim(I)≤a for all a>1 and therefore hdim(I)≤1.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"Hmeasure\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"hdim(I)≤1.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"hdim\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Fix δ>0 and any countable δ-cover W of I, and set ρ_i=diam W_i≤δ. For arbitrary ε>0, enclose each nonempty W_i in J_i=(inf W_i-ε2^{-i-2},sup W_i+ε2^{-i-2}); its endpoints are finite because W_i is nonempty and bounded. Its length is at most ρ_i+ε2^{-i-1}; set J_i=∅ for empty W_i. The J_i cover I. By M007, the length of I is 1; monotonicity and M006 give 1≤Σ_i|J_i|. M008 bounds this by Σ_iρ_i+Σ_iε2^{-i-1}=Σ_iρ_i+ε. If Σ_iρ_i is infinite the claimed bound is immediate; otherwise let ε↓0 to get Σ_iρ_i≥1. Close the arbitrary choices to conclude that for every δ>0, every countable δ-cover of I has sum of diameters at least one.\",\"uses\":[\"M006\",\"M007\",\"M008\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"δ\",\"ε\",\"W\",\"ρ\",\"J\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"For every δ>0 and every countable cover W of I with diam W_i≤δ, Σ_i diam W_i≥1.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"δ\",\"type\":\"positive real\"},{\"symbol\":\"W\",\"type\":\"sequence of subsets of ℝ\"}],\"objects\":[\"δ\",\"W\",\"I\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"For any 0<s<1 and any δ-cover of I with diameters ρ_i≤δ, one has ρ_i^s≥δ^{s-1}ρ_i; at ρ_i=0 both sides are zero, and for ρ_i>0 this follows since the exponent s-1 is negative. Thus F002 gives Σ_iρ_i^s≥δ^{s-1}Σ_iρ_i≥δ^{s-1}. Taking the infimum over covers yields Hscale(s,δ,I)≥δ^{s-1}→∞ as δ↓0. Hence Hmeasure(s,I)=∞ and N001 gives hdim(I)≥s for every 0<s<1. Let s↑1 to obtain hdim(I)≥1, which together with F001 proves hdim(I)=1.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"hdim(I)=1.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"hdim\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"Suppose D=0. Choose x_0∈E by H001 and define φ:I→F by φ(t)=(x_0,t). The Euclidean distance formula gives dist(φ(t),φ(u))=|t-u|, so this is an isometric embedding, also when n=0. To justify the dimension monotonicity being used, pull back any δ-cover of F under φ. Its preimages cover I, and every preimage has diameter at most that of the corresponding covering member: distances of preimage points equal distances of their images. Empty preimages contribute zero. Thus Hscale(a,δ,I)≤Hscale(a,δ,F) for all a>0 and δ>0, and taking suprema gives Hmeasure(a,I)≤Hmeasure(a,F). By F003 and N001, Hmeasure(a,I)=∞ for every 0<a<1, hence Hmeasure(a,F)=∞ and hdim(F)≥a. Let a↑1 to get hdim(F)≥1=hdim(I). Since D=0 this is 1=D+1. N002 ensures the finite-real interpretation of D, and no step required n>0. Discharge D=0 to prove N006.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"N001\",\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"E\",\"n\",\"x_0\",\"φ\",\"I\",\"F\",\"Hscale\",\"Hmeasure\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[\"L2\"]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M006\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"Set α=ℝ, ι=ℕ, G=the type of Borel measures on ℝ, μ=Lebesgue measure and T_i=J_i.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Measures evaluate sets as extended nonnegative numbers and have the canonical FunLike and OuterMeasureClass structures; Lebesgue measure is such a measure.\",\"The index type is ℕ, which is countable.\"]},{\"input\":\"M007\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"Set a=0,b=1, giving the measure of I.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]},{\"input\":\"M008\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"For each nonempty W_i set a=inf W_i-ε2^{-i-2}, b=sup W_i+ε2^{-i-2}; these are the endpoints of J_i. Empty J_i have measure zero separately.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[]}]},{\"id\":\"R007\",\"inputs\":[\"N002\",\"N003\",\"N005\",\"N006\"],\"output\":\"P\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D005\",\"D006\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"case_elimination\"],\"locals\":[],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"By N002, 0≤D≤n, so D is finite and either D>0 or D=0. In the first case N005 gives hdim(F)≥D+1; in the second N006 gives exactly the same lower bound. Thus hdim(F)≥D+1 in all cases. N003 gives the reverse bound. By antisymmetry hdim(F)=D+1=hdim(E)+1, as required. The definition of F supplies precisely E×[0,1] in the Euclidean metric, including n=0.\",\"uses\":[\"N002\",\"N003\",\"N005\",\"N006\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"D\",\"n\",\"E\",\"F\",\"hdim\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"]}],\"applications\":[]}]}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additio